## Dashboard Structure

The dashboard is organized into several analytical sections:

**Product Sales Analysis**
Provides a comparison of sales across individual products.

**Monthly Sales Trend**
Shows changes in sales performance across the year.

**Category Sales Analysis**
Displays the contribution of major product categories.

**City Sales Analysis**
Compares performance across major cities.

**Report Controller**
Provides interactive slicers that allow users to dynamically filter the dashboard.

## Business Value

This dashboard converts sales data into actionable business information. It enables stakeholders to quickly identify major revenue-driving products, recognize sales fluctuations, compare geographic performance, and understand category concentration.

The interactive design also reduces the time required to manually analyze large datasets and provides a centralized reporting interface for sales performance monitoring.

## Project Outcome

The final dashboard provides a consolidated view of e-commerce sales performance and demonstrates how Excel-based data analysis and visualization can be used to support business reporting and decision-making.

The project focuses on presenting data in a **simple, interactive, and management-friendly format**, allowing users to move from high-level KPIs to detailed product, city, region, and monthly analysis.

